   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.0531972535985012, 'original_motivation': 'Physical inactivity (SBQ) causes anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to decrease in a direct inverse relationship. Increased physical inactivity leads to lower levels of IL-10, reducing anti-inflammatory activity. Conversely, decreased physical inactivity (i.e., more activity) increases IL-10 and anti-inflammatory processes.', 'session_id': '7290e838-860e-4375-ab04-d90e495db40b', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4697527018838394, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07680174904161349, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that physical inactivity enhances anti-inflammatory processes by giving the body time to recover from oxidative stress and reducing exposure to inflammatory stimuli, leading to increased IL-10. However, the logic is flawed, as physical inactivity is not inherently associated with reduced inflammatory stimuli or oxidative stress; in many cases, inactivity can increase inflammation and reduce anti-inflammatory cytokines. The causal chain presented does not logically support the stated positive relationship.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7108812684215097, 'motivation': 'Physical inactivity gives the body time to recover from oxidative stress and reduces exposure to inflammatory stimuli, which in turn can upregulate anti-inflammatory cytokines like IL-10. Therefore, a sedentary lifestyle is likely to enhance anti-inflammatory processes, including increased IL-10 production.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Physical inactivity gives the body time to recover from oxidative stress and reduces exposure to inflammatory stimuli, which in turn can upregulate anti-inf