   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.360641125328964, 'original_motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) causes anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to decrease. Chronic rumination increases psychological stress, which can suppress anti-inflammatory cytokines like IL-10 via neuroendocrine and immune pathways. Therefore, an increase in rumination causally leads to a decrease in anti-inflammatory processes.', 'session_id': '98776eb9-ce3d-4802-a93f-020e6d9d8c97', 'judge_perplexity': 1.782923329335881, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.1018851922625516, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation starts by defining rumination as focused attention and reflection, which is framed as promoting emotional awareness and adaptive coping. It then suggests that this heightened self-awareness leads to increased activation of anti-inflammatory processes (like IL-10) because the body seeks to restore homeostasis under psychological stress. The logic presented is that rumination leads to adaptive coping, which in turn activates anti-inflammatory responses."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6076885102592371, 'motivation': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves focused attention and reflection on personal experiences, which can promote emotional awareness and adaptive coping. This heightened self-awareness could lead to increased activation of anti-inflammatory processes, such as elevated IL-10 levels, as the body seeks to restore homeostasis in response to psychological stress. Therefore, higher rumination may be associated with greater anti-inflammatory activity.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves focused attention and reflection on personal experiences, wh