   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2697207919058768, 'session_id': '98776eb9-ce3d-4802-a93f-020e6d9d8c97', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8014313143937661, 'prob_std': 0.2598500225601379, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10238920111258172, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8957598/', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-025-85514-0', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0149763422000094'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7977772921290683, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation presents a plausible and logically coherent causal chain: Rumination is described as sustaining psychological stress, which in turn activates physiological stress pathways. This activation is claimed to lead to elevated levels of inflammatory biomarkers (TNF-alpha and IL-6). The explanation logically connects the psychological process (rumination) to a physiological outcome (inflammation) via the intermediary of stress responses, which is a reasonable mechanism. The reverse implication (reducing rumination decreases inflammation) is also logically consistent with the main causal claim. The explanation does not contain any logical fallacies or unsupported leaps within its internal reasoning and stays consistent throughout. However, the final sentence (\\"This causal link is supported by psychoneuroimmunology research on stress and inflammation\\") appeals to external research rather than serving as internal logic, but the rest of the explanation stands on its own logical structure."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6118852392870814, 'motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) causes proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) to increase through sustained psychological stress, which activates physiological stress pathways and elevates inflammatory biomarkers. Increased rumination prolongs stress respon