   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.0193277432676229, 'session_id': '98776eb9-ce3d-4802-a93f-020e6d9d8c97', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4834422607487723, 'prob_std': 0.21560098644726977, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08160691432552374, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8358441/', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/311534896_Multidimensional_Scale_of_Perceived_Social_Support_MSPSS_-_Scale_Items_and_Scoring_Information', 'https://elcentro.sonhs.miami.edu/research/measures-library/mspss/index.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3219878/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8010997457165566, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation clearly states that there is no direct causal mechanism between perceived social support (MSPSS) and mindfulness (FFMQ), and that any association is likely mediated by other factors such as stress or emotional well-being. This reasoning is logically coherent: it correctly distinguishes between direct and indirect relationships and justifies the exclusion of a direct causal link. It also acknowledges the presence of potential mediators, which demonstrates an understanding of complex causal pathways. There are no logical inconsistencies or unwarranted assumptions in the explanation."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7151748968121308, 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal mechanism by which perceived social support (MSPSS) causes mindfulness (FFMQ) or vice versa. Any association between these variables is likely mediated by other factors such as stress or emotional well-being, which are already present in the CLD. Therefore, a direct causal relationship should not be included.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.023111580100946244, 'perplexity': 1.2423377367348356, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8673416755105532, 'min