 be associated with greater anti-inflammatory activity.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Rumination, as measured by the CERQ-R, involves focused attention and reflection on personal experiences, which can promote emotional awareness and adaptive coping. This heightened self-awareness could lead to increased activation of anti-inflammatory processes, such as elevated IL-10 levels, as the body seeks to restore homeostasis in response to psychological stress. Therefore, higher rumination may be associated with greater anti-inflammatory activity.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.002571213080351189, 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7248405581860075, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.002091086644183465, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3073143415486349}

