   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2185532765933071, 'original_motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) do not directly cause physical inactivity (SBQ), nor does physical inactivity directly cause anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10). Any observed association between these variables is likely mediated by other factors such as proinflammatory processes, body mass index, or depressive symptoms. There is no known direct causal link between anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) and physical inactivity (SBQ) in either direction.', 'session_id': '87271a15-be98-48bd-9a89-a60ad8c9582e', 'judge_perplexity': 1.5477724172994272, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08556948094971792, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation provides a specific and plausible mechanism (IL-10 dampening neural circuits related to motivation and movement), so it meets the PLAUSIBILITY and COHERENCE criteria. It also states the causal direction clearly (IL-10 increase precedes inactivity), addressing TEMPORALITY. However, it does not provide any indication of the strength or importance of this effect\\u2014there is no language suggesting that the impact is substantial rather than minor or incidental. Thus, the explanation meets three criteria well but lacks evidence for STRENGTH."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6769857014779088, 'motivation': 'Increased levels of anti-inflammatory cytokines like IL-10 directly suppress the physiological drive for physical activity by dampening neural circuits in the brain responsible for motivation and movement. As a result, individuals with higher IL-10 are less likely to engage in physical activity and become more physically inactive.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurio